{"id":12000,"date":"2025-03-28T21:34:16","date_gmt":"2025-03-28T21:34:16","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=12000"},"modified":"2025-08-29T10:12:32","modified_gmt":"2025-08-29T10:12:32","slug":"cheap-remodeling","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/cheap-remodeling\/","title":{"rendered":"The Truth About Cheap Remodeling Bids You Need To Hear"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remodeling your home is an exciting investment, but it comes with big decisions. One of the most important is choosing the right contractor. When faced with multiple bids, the temptation to go with a cheap remodeling option can be strong. After all, saving money upfront feels like a win. But what if that &#8220;savings&#8221; ends up costing you more in the long run? By understanding the pitfalls and embracing the Oregon Preconstruction Process, you can ensure your remodel is stress-free and successful.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are looking for a more in-depth and personal discussion with our team regarding your specific project, feel free to book a hassle free, no obligation 1 on 1 virtual consultation with our Construction Consultant:<a href=\"https:\/\/api.leadconnectorhq.com\/widget\/bookings\/harris-sons-virtual-consultation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"\">&nbsp;<strong>Book a Call.<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXdGOAWr2pdFatRqYtg2A-HqX0AMblr3CGJI3YzTmeMvzWMfz1mQP8gYLcR0t49vJAaFkba5huiMOTXbtTCT1ckZcnwMZQPCFOF0GbvRAEnRaPxxl-kZNHmo1mPXeVJjFTkjM4ADsg.png\" alt=\"cheap remodeling\" class=\"wp-image-12005\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why Homeowners Are Drawn to Cheap Remodeling Bids<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It\u2019s easy to understand why low bids are attractive. Common reasons homeowners choose them include:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Budget Concerns:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tight budgets make cheaper options seem like the best choice.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Assumption of Similarity:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many homeowners believe all contractors deliver the same results, so the cheapest one seems like better value.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Eagerness to Start:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The desire to kick off the project quickly often leads to hasty decisions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While these are valid concerns, the cheapest bid often hides significant risks that can lead to stress, delays, and far higher costs than anticipated. By incorporating the Oregon Preconstruction Process, you can avoid these pitfalls.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Hidden Costs of Cheap Remodeling Bids<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cheap bids often omit critical components or rely on cost-cutting measures that come back to haunt homeowners. Here are the most common hidden costs:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Cheap Materials That Don\u2019t Last<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Explanation:<\/strong> Contractors offering low bids frequently cut corners by using subpar materials. While these may look fine initially, they wear out or fail quickly, leaving you with expensive repairs or replacements.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A homeowner chooses a cheap contractor for new flooring, only to find it warping after a year due to poor-quality materials.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Unaccounted-for Change Orders<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Explanation:<\/strong> Low bids may exclude important tasks or details, leading to mid-project \u201cchange orders.\u201d These additional expenses can significantly inflate the final price.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A contractor\u2019s low bid for a kitchen remodel didn\u2019t include rewiring for new appliances. The homeowner had to pay thousands more to fix the oversight.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Delays and Extended Timelines<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Explanation:<\/strong> Low-bid contractors often overbook projects or fail to plan adequately, leading to delays that disrupt your life.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A family\u2019s living room remodel dragged on for months because their contractor was juggling too many jobs at once.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Skipping Permits and Code Compliance<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Explanation:<\/strong> To save time and money, some contractors skip obtaining permits or ignore building codes. This can lead to fines, legal issues, or even the need to redo the work entirely.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A homeowner saved upfront by skipping permits but later had to pay hefty fines and redo work that wasn\u2019t up to code. For permit guidelines, visit Oregon Permit Resources.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. Low-Quality Work That Needs Fixing<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Explanation:<\/strong> Shoddy workmanship is a hallmark of low-bid projects. What seems like a deal at first often results in costly repairs or replacements later.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A rushed basement remodel resulted in improper waterproofing, leading to significant water damage and repair costs.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXe2Bfs0dziorY85vxTXiHBn0PYHbi759kMSF0IOzQqgLrXqQuGgM5RnRCs5y96_tmF0r6_zcrjewP2yRGZgxm80YqXQXjs-vm0ssSaMOKT_kl6fNxcrm_Q4EwBDquD1JooVaagj.png\" alt=\"unlicensed contractors vs pros\" class=\"wp-image-12004\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What to Look Out For in Cheap Remodeling Bids<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If a bid seems too good to be true, it likely is. Watch out for these red flags:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Vague Contracts:<\/strong> Missing details about materials, timelines, or specific tasks.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Unrealistic Timelines:<\/strong> Promises that seem overly quick compared to other estimates.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Lack of References:<\/strong> Difficulty providing reviews or past client testimonials.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>No Mention of Permits:<\/strong> Skipping this step can lead to serious legal and safety issues.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why Proper Planning Prevents Hidden Costs<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The key to avoiding the pitfalls of cheap bids is proper preconstruction planning. Every homeowner deserves a remodeling process that\u2019s transparent, thorough, and free from nasty surprises. This is where the Oregon Preconstruction Process shines.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is Preconstruction?<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preconstruction is the planning phase where every detail of your project is mapped out. It includes budgeting, design, timelines, and permits, ensuring the entire remodel runs smoothly from start to finish. For an in-depth overview, visit Preconstruction Explained.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Preconstruction Benefits You<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Transparent Budgets:<\/strong>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>You\u2019ll know exactly what you\u2019re paying for upfront, reducing the risk of unplanned expenses.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>No Surprises:<\/strong>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Potential challenges are identified and addressed before construction begins.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Efficient Timelines:<\/strong>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>A clear schedule ensures your project is completed on time.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Guaranteed Compliance:<\/strong>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Permits and building codes are handled professionally, giving you peace of mind.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Real-Life Example: Cheap vs. Planned Remodeling<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Risk of Going Cheap<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A homeowner in Oregon hired the lowest-bid contractor for a bathroom remodel. Halfway through, they discovered the contractor hadn\u2019t accounted for plumbing upgrades. The final cost ended up $8,000 over budget, and the project took three months longer than expected.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Value of Planning<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Another homeowner invested in a contractor who prioritized preconstruction. The detailed budget and timeline meant no surprises, and the high-quality materials ensured the finished remodel exceeded expectations. The project was completed on time and added significant value to their home.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Bottom Line for Homeowners<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Choosing a contractor isn\u2019t just about the price\u2014it\u2019s about value. Cheap remodeling bids may save money upfront, but the hidden costs can far outweigh the initial savings. Proper planning through the Oregon Preconstruction Process ensures your project is stress-free, stays within budget, and delivers results you\u2019ll love for years to come.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Your Next Step<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Avoid the risks of cheap remodeling bids and hidden costs. Choose a contractor who prioritizes planning, quality, and transparency.<a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\"> Contact us today<\/a> to learn more about how the Oregon Preconstruction Process ensures your remodel is done right the first time. Let\u2019s make your dream home a reality\u2014without the stress or surprises.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Remodeling your home is an exciting investment, but it comes with big decisions. One of the most important is choosing the right contractor. When faced with multiple bids, the temptation to go with a cheap remodeling option can be strong. After all, saving money upfront feels like a win. But what if that &#8220;savings&#8221; ends [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":12002,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[31,36,38,33,39],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-12000","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-contractors-guides","category-general","category-remodel","category-remodeling-tips","category-resources"],"acf":[],"_lin